{
 "id": "nema17-mount-stl",
 "brief": "I need a bracket that holds a NEMA 17 stepper (motor-body.stl is the motor body, attached, in\nmillimetres, already placed where it sits: its body is y = 5 to 53) onto a flat plate. PETG, FDM,\nprinted with the base on the bed (layers along +Z). The bracket's face plate goes against the\nmotor's front face, between y = 0 and 5; the rest of the bracket may wrap round the motor body\n(but not into it) to reach the base screws. The four M3 face screws are on a 31 mm square\ncentred on the shaft at (0, 0, 35) and run along Y, so the holes are at x = +/-15.5,\nz = 19.5 and 50.5; each needs a 4.5 mm radius pad 5 mm thick (y = 0 to 5). The 22 mm pilot\nboss on the motor face needs a 23 mm hole with a 1.5 mm ring round it. The bracket screws down\nto the plate (z = 0) with two M4 screws along Z at (+/-15, 35), each with a 6 mm radius,\n5 mm tall boss, and I need a screwdriver to reach those screws from above (keep a 9 mm diameter\ncolumn clear above each). It has to fit in x = -25 to 25, y = 0 to 50, z = 0 to 62. The belt\npulls the shaft with up to 60 N, mostly upward (+Z) but it can also pull sideways along X.\nThe motor is 350 g. Safety factor 2.",
